    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. its not even a plateau, its just a ceiling. i can see it clearly now. everything i do from here on out is just... padding time. pretending that being 'fine' or 'decent' is enough is just a lie we tell ourselves to keep going. but if the spark is gone, and i know i'll never be great, what's the point of the rest of the performance? it just feels like staying in a room where the lights have already gone out.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
